cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LogitGate in your research or production systems, please cite it as below."
title: "LogitGate: Calibrated First-Token Logit Evaluation and Cascaded Routing for LLMs"
version: 0.4.1
date-released: "2026-11-10"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jasonbdly/LogitGate"
url: "https://github.com/jasonbdly/LogitGate"
abstract: >-
  LogitGate is a lightweight, 3-layer cascaded LLM evaluation and routing
  library. It reduces autoregressive judge latency and mitigates token prior
  and positional biases through symmetric first-token log-odds calibration,
  shared-prefix KV-cache prompt compilation, and deterministic AST/contract checks.
authors:
  - family-names: "Bradley"
    given-names: "Jason"
    email: "jasonbdly@gmail.com"
keywords:
  - "large-language-models"
  - "llm-as-a-judge"
  - "logprobs"
  - "logit-calibration"
  - "cascaded-routing"
  - "prefix-caching"
  - "system-1-evaluation"
